Implementing the System
1. Attach Inventory.cs to the target character.
2. Drag And drop Inventory Canvas from the prefabs. This is the Canvas used to interact with the inventory.
3. Add InventoryUI.cs to the Scroll View of the Inventory Canvas
    - UI Item Prefab: general UI Item Prefab that is in the Prefabs/Items folder
    - Inventory: Drag The Game Object which has the inventory
    - UI Inventory Panel: Drag the InventoryCanvas/InventoryScrollView/ViewPort/Content there
4. On the game Object that has the inventory:
    - UI: Drag the InventoryScrollView into it
    - AudioSource: Drag an audio source in it (prefferably attached to the character i guess)
    - Dropped Item Prefab: Prefab/Items/"Dropped Item Prefab"
    - Pick Up Item Audio: Drag the audio clip you want played when the item is picked up
    - Drop Item Audio: Same thing


Creating An Item
1. Create Item through create option in the unity dropdown. It is Under Item -> Item. Put it inside the Prefabs/"Item Data" folder.
2. Create the item prefab you want to use. It needs to have a Collider2D that is disabled.
    - Add DroppedItem.cs to the prefab
        * Pickup Delay: timer to prevent instant pickup
        * Item: The Item you created inside Item Data folder in step one.
    - Give it the DroppedItem tag
3. Inside the Item from step 1
    - Give it an ID
    - Give Description
    - Icon: Drag the item sprite inside it
    - Prefab: Drag the prefab you created in step 2

4. When Placing the item in the world, Enable the Collider2D

